{"path":"algorithm/ranges/unique_copy","title":"std::ranges::unique_copy, std::ranges::unique_copy_result","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::</span>unique_copy, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::</span>unique_copy_result","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/unique_copy","section":"algorithm","kind":"page","summary":"The function-like entities described on this page are algorithm function objects (informally known as niebloids), that is:","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/algorithm\">&lt;algorithm&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-h\">\n<td> <div>Call signature</div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/input_iterator\"><span class=\"kw2882\">std::<span class=\"me2\">input_iterator</span></span></a> I, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/sentinel_for\"><span class=\"kw2880\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sentinel_for</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>I<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> S, <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/weakly_incrementable\"><span class=\"kw2877\">std::<span class=\"me2\">weakly_incrementable</span></span></a> O,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> Proj <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/functional/identity\"><span class=\"kw2741\">std::<span class=\"me2\">identity</span></span></a>,<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/indirect_equivalence_relation\"><span class=\"kw3139\">std::<span class=\"me2\">indirect_equivalence_relation</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/projected\"><span class=\"kw2695\">projected</span></a><s